ct-statement-for-primar-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-rm8fhrtwr4qbkhyh","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Which of the following is not a correct statement for primary aliphatic amines?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The intermolecular association in primary amines is less than the intermolecular association in secondary amines."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Primary amines on treating with nitrous acid solution from corresponding alcohols except mythyl amine."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Primary amines are less basic than the secondary amines."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Primary amines can be prepared by the Gabriel phthalimide synthesis."}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The intermolecular association is more prominent in case of primary amines as compared to secondary, due to the availability of two hydrogen atom."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा प्राथमिक अलिफैटिक अमाइन्स के लिए सही कथन नहीं है?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"प्राथमिक अमीनों में अंतराण्वयिक संघनन द्वितीयक अमीनों में अंतराण्वयिक संघनन से कम होता है।"},{"identifier":"B","content":"प्राथमिक अमाइन्स को नाइत्रस अम्ल के घोल के साथ उपचारित करने पर संबंधित अल्कोहल्स बनते हैं सिवाय मिथाइल अमीन के।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"प्राथमिक अमीन द्वितीयक अमाइन्स की तुलना में कम मूलीय होते हैं।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"प्राथमिक अमीन्स को गेब्रियल फथालिमाइड संश्लेषण द्वारा तैयार किया जा सकता है।"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"aliphatic-amines","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-27th-august-morning-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-27th-august-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1ktebydcv","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 27th August Morning Shift","permalink":"acidic-ferric-chloride-solution-on-treatment-with-excess-of-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-49flw433fowijhto","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Acidic ferric chloride solution on treatment with excess of potassium ferrocyanide gives a Prussian blue coloured colloidal species. It is :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Fe<sub>4</sub>[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"K<sub>5</sub>Fe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"HFe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]"},{"identifier":"D","content":"KFe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Prussian blue is a complex compound that has the formula <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.081ex\" height=\"2.265ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 6665.7 1000.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1233,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1636.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1914.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe(CN)</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(3633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(5951.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(311,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. It is formed by the reaction of ferric ions with ferrocyanide ions.</p>\n<p>The reaction can be explained as follows:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Potassium ferrocyanide, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.736ex\" height=\"2.265ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 5629.1 1000.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">K</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1036.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1314.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe(CN)</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(3633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5351.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, dissociates in water to release ferrocyanide ions, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.623ex\" height=\"2.472ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -841.7 5579.2 1092.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(278,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe(CN)</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(3633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(4314.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(311,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n</li><br>\n<li><p>The ferric ions, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.947ex\" height=\"2.596ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -947.3 2186.7 1147.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1233,477.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, present in the acidic ferric chloride solution will react with the ferrocyanide ions.</p>\n</li><br>\n<li><p>In an acidic medium, the ferric ions hydrolyze, forming a complex with ferrocyanide ions, leading to the formation of Prussian blue.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The overall reaction can be represented as:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"40.067ex\" height=\"2.711ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -947.3 17709.6 1198.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1233,477.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2408.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3409.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3909.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4187.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe(CN)</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(3633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(8223.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(311,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9766.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(11043.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1233,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(12680.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(12958.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Fe(CN)</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(3633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(16995,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(311,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>The Prussian blue complex is a colloidal species and exhibits an intense blue color. It has been historically used as a pigment in paints and also has applications in medical treatments as an antidote for certain types of heavy metal poisoning.</p>\n"},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"एसिडिक फेरिक क्लोराइड समाधान को पोटेशियम फेरोसायनाइड के अधिकता के साथ उपचार करने पर प्रशियन नीले रंग की कोलायडियल प्रजाति प्राप्त होती है। वह है :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Fe<sub>4</sub>[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"K<sub>5</sub>Fe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"HFe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]"},{"identifier":"D","content":"KFe[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"chemistry-involved-in-the-preparation-of-organic-and-inorganic-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-27th-august-morning-shift","isOutOf